      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ec1c68fa-5233-4608-86f3-b71ac2abe7ba",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 12,
      "data": {
        "title": "Exemplos de CLI"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "2503dd23-0319-498c-afee-94c0622c1a29",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "language": "bash",
            "code": "# Criar VPC\naws ec2 create-vpc --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/16\n\n# Criar subnet pública\naws ec2 create-subnet --vpc-id vpc-abc \\\n  --cidr-block 10.0.1.0/24 \\\n  --availability-zone sa-east-1a\n\n# Security Group permitindo SSH só de um IP\naws ec2 create-security-group \\\n  --group-name bastion-sg \\\n  --description \"SSH from office\" \\\n  --vpc-id vpc-abc\naws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \\\n  --group-id sg-xyz \\\n  --protocol tcp --port 22 \\\n  --cidr 203.0.113.42/32\n\n# Route 53 — criar um registro A\naws route53 change-resource-record-sets \\\n  --hosted-zone-id Z1234 \\\n  --change-batch file://change.json"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "79c3213d-00f9-419d-aa02-033b84f30571",
      "type": "callout",
      "position": 13,
      "data": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "title": "",
        "content": "Pegadinha: \"VPC Peering é transitivo?\" — Não. Se A peering B e B peering C, A NÃO fala com C. Para conectar múltiplas VPCs, use Transit Gateway."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "64da77c8-287a-40e4-a7e9-c19a81f8367a",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 14,
      "data": {
        "title": "Perguntas típicas (Q&A)"
      },
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "df124e05-4674-49e9-abb4-dd76a4816424",
      "type": "callout",
      "position": 15,
      "data": {
        "variant": "success",
        "title": "",
        "content": "Take-aways: VPC = rede isolada por Região. Subnet = por AZ. Pública (rota → IGW) vs privada (rota → NAT). SG = stateful na ENI. NACL = stateless na subnet. Route 53 = DNS + 7 policies. CloudFront = CDN em 600+ Edges. Global Accelerator = anycast TCP/UDP. VPC Endpoint = acesso privado a serviços AWS. DX = fibra dedicada. ALB/NLB/GWLB por camada."
      }
    }
  ]
